      "content": "That feeling of being a relic, of being too much or too little for this current moment, is a very heavy thing to carry. You are not just taking up space; you are a collection of experiences that this new, fast-moving world can't process. If the effort of trying to grasp onto something feels like a constant, draining fight, maybe the most honest thing you can do is stop fighting. Just let the weight of it all settle, and see what happens when you stop trying to fit the mold.",
